{%- comment -%}
  Authorization policy: public_read (Layer-2, app-owned; spec §12.2).

  Permits any AUTHENTICATED principal to invoke the tool. This is an EXPLICIT allow
  named in the manifest — there is no implicit/anonymous permit path, so even
  "public" read access is a visible, reviewed decision (§12.2). The engine has
  already resolved a real identity before this runs; a caller with no valid token
  never reaches policy evaluation.

  Contract: return true / false, or { allow, reason }. Receives principal, agent,
  arguments, tool, delegation_mode.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign r = '{}' | parse_json
  hash_assign r['allow'] = true
  hash_assign r['reason'] = 'public_read'
  return r
%}
